===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|klawe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|klāwa}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*klawō}}. Compare {{cog|nl|klauw}}, {{cog|en|claw}}, {{cog|da|klo}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f,n}}

# [[claw]], [[talon]]
#: {{syn|de|Kralle}}
# [[cloven hoof]]
# {{lb|de|figurative|chiefly|in the plural}} [[control]]
#: {{uxi|de|den '''Klauen''' des Todes entweichen}}
#: {{uxi|de|jemanden in den '''Klauen''' haben}}
#: {{uxi|de|jemandem in die '''Klauen''' fallen}}
# {{lb|de|slang|chiefly|derogatory|figurative}} [[hand]]
#: {{syn|de|Kralle|Flosse|Pfote}}
#: {{uxi|de|Nimm deine schmutzigen '''Klauen''' weg!}}
# {{lb|de|slang|derogatory}} [[chicken scratch]] {{gloss|poor handwriting}}
#: {{syn|de|Sauklaue}}
# part of hook-like shape, especially with the purpose of grasping, gripping
## triangular recess at the junction of two beams
## a projection on a machine part which, when engaged or engaged in a correspondingly shaped recess in another machine part, makes a detachable connection with the latter

